    "question": {
      "en": "If $4^x = 5^y = 20^z$, then find $\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y}$.",
      "hi": "यदि $4^x = 5^y = 20^z$ है, तो $\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y}$ ज्ञात कीजिए।"
    },
    "options": "(a) $1/z$ &emsp; (b) $z$ &emsp; (c) $2/z$ &emsp; (d) 1",
    "solution": {
      "en": "Let $4^x = 5^y = 20^z = k \\implies 4 = k^{1/x}$, $5 = k^{1/y}$, $20 = k^{1/z}$.<br>Since $4 \\times 5 = 20 \\implies k^{1/x} \\times k^{1/y} = k^{1/z} \\implies \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} = \\mathbf{\\frac{1}{z}}$.<br><br><strong>Answer: (a) 1/z</strong>",
      "hi": "मान लीजिए $4^x = 5^y = 20^z = k \\implies 4 = k^{1/x}, 5 = k^{1/y}, 20 = k^{1/z}$।<br>चूंकि $4 \\times 5 = 20 \\implies k^{1/x + 1/y} = k^{1/z} \\implies \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} = \\mathbf{\\frac{1}{z}}$ है।<br><br><strong>उत्तर: (a) 1/z</strong>"
    }
  },
